<title>GREECE: Greek TEB announces lower 96 profit.</title>
<headline>Greek TEB announces lower 96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek construction company TEB said its 1996 turnover rose 23.8 percent to 8.00 billion drachmas from 6.46 billion a year earlier but profits dropped 9 percent to 1.0 billion drachmas from 1.1 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>TEB's orderbook of uncompleted projects stands at 55 billion drachmas, the company told Reuters in a statement.</p>
<p>TEB said it had submitted offers for projects worth a total of 88.8 bln drs that were still pending.</p>
<p>Its shares closed at 1,700 drachmas on Friday, up 40 drachmas.</p>
<p>--Margarita Sotiropoulou, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
